ÄPrez poslednite chetiri godini s'r Aleks F'rgius'n e razmishliaval nad v'rkhovite momenti ot svoiata izkliuchitelna kariera i si e vodil belezhki. Tuk toi razkriva svoiata izumitelna istoriia, taka kakto tia se e sluchila v razvitie oshche ot negovata ranna v'zrast i tezhkiia zhivot v korabostroitelnite kvartali na Gov'n. S'r Aleks opovestiava svoeto ottegliane ot posta menidzh'r na Manchest'r Iunaited, sled kato v prod'lzhenie na dvadeset i sedem godini izp'lniava tazi dl'zhnost. Toi si tr'gna po slaven nachin, kato zavoiuva titlata na Visshata liga s Iunaited za trinaiseti p't. Mnozina go smiatat za nai-velikiia menidzh'r v istoriiata na britanskiia futbol. Prez posledniia chetv'rt vek Manchest'r Iunaited e preminaval prez razt'rsvashchi promeni, kato edinstvenata postoianna velichina e kachestvoto na otbora, s koito menidzh'ra pecheli Ligata, i nesekvashchata poreditsa ot uspekhi."ë
é"Tikhoto sl'ntse" e roman eksperiment. Roman za edin glas, koito otseliava sled fizicheskata sm'rt i razkazva istoriiata na choveka, koito prezhiviava vsichki zabrani prez tialoto si.
"Maistorstvoto na Pet'r Denchev e v sposobnostta mu vseobkhvatno da opishe i t'lkuva edna metafizicheska, a vs'shchnost napravo fizicheska zaplakha. Tazi pretsizna politicheska protsedura na "Tikhoto sl'ntse" obache ni nai-malko ne snema naprezhenieto v teksta. Um't na Pet'r Denchev ne oblekchava nikogo. I tova, koeto toi predveshchava kato koshmar za tsialoto obshchestvo, e veche realnost v'v vseki edin ot nas.
Stiga da si otvorim ushite, razbira se."
Marin Bodakov"í
èKasi raboti kato servit'orka v Niu Orli'ns i vsiaka vecher bavno tr'gva k'm doma si, k'm ednostainoto si zhilishche, samotata i t'gata. No v denia, v koito namira zabraven ot misteriozna nepoznata belezhnik zhivot't i se promenia zavinagi. Tova, koeto prochita v belezhnika, e i potresavashcho, i shokirashcho, i interesno, i s'vsem razlichno ot sveta, v koito zhivee, i v kraina smetka ia otvezhda do S.E.K.R.E.T. - taina obshchnost, koiato pomaga na zheni kato Kasi da os'shchestviat nai-intimnite si, nai-s'krovenite si seksualni fantazii. Kasi se vpuska v ludo p'teshestvie prez deset udivitelni fantazii s krasivi, s'blaznitelni, silni m'zhe, koito probuzhdat tialoto i i i pokazvat strani na udovolstvieto, koito nikoga ne e poznavala. Kasi bavno, no s's sigurni st'pki se osvobozhdava ot kompleksite i strakhovete si i otkriva v sebe si edna uverena, preobrazena zhena. Tazi zhena i dava smelostta da zhivee s nast'rvenost i strast. Osvobozhdavashcha i predizvikatelna ,,S.E.K.R.E.T." shche vi razkrie edin sviat, v koito mechtite i fantaziite se prevr'shchat v realnost.
S.E.K.R.E.T - L. Mari Adelin
Sk'pi priiateli,
Iskate da nadniknete zad S.E.K.R.E.T.-noto? A mozhete li da pazite taina? Ot dosta vreme s'm v tozi biznes, no sega s ogromna radost i udovletvorenie moga da vi s'obshchia, che misteriiata skoro shche b'de razbulena. D'rzhite v r'tsete si knigata, koiato s'budi svetoven interes i razpali ozhestocheni diskusii. Tova e p'rvata kniga ot edna poreditsa inteligentna erotika ot s'vsem novo pokolenie.
Tazi poreditsa v'znikna v otgovor na v'pros, koito diskutirakhme s avtora na knigata: kato se ima predvid strastniiat otklik ot strana na chitatelskata auditoriia k'm erotikata, dali e v'zmozhno da se napishe roman, koito da e predi vsichko interesna, dobre zamislena i inteligentno i plenitelno pres'zdadena istoriia i v dop'lnenie k'm tova da b'de zareden s moshchen seksualen zariad i kak chitatelite bikha prieli edna takava kniga v usloviiata na segashniia izdatelski klimat.
L. Mari Adelin vi predlaga kniga, chiito stil mozhe da se opishe kato visoko inteligenten, izt'nchen i plenitelen, s maistorski izgradeni kharakteri ot pl't i kr'v, s zhivopisni opisaniia na mesta i s'bitiia i edna naistina zavladiavashcha istoriia. Svet't posreshchna knigata s edno goliamo i ubeditelno ,,Da!". ,,S.E.K.R.E.T." pomete kato taifun panaira na knigata v'v Frankfurt i samo za niakolko sedmitsi pravata za izdavane na knigata biakha prodadeni v nad triiset strani.
S kakvo se otlichava tazi poreditsa ot vsichko, koeto ste cheli dosega? S tova, che zhenite pritezhavat sila i reshitelnost, geroite - kakto zhenite, taka i m'zhete - sa khora kato samite vas, realni i zemni. Razbira se, ima seks, i to dosta provokativen (inak ne bi bilo erotika), no osnovnata nishka v tozi roman e p'tiat obratno k'm sebe si: da namerish silata i onezi kachestva, za koito ne si podoziral, che s'shchestvuvat v samiia teb, da se probudish za edin po-iar'k i dori shemeten zhivot, koito bi te napravil shchastliv.
Nadiavam se svet't na ,,S.E.K.R.E.T." da vi dade imenno tova i prikliuchenieto da vi dostavi radost i naslada.
Priemate li St'pka edno?
Nina Pronovost
Glaven redaktor
Doubleday Canada Publishing Group"£
†The word "globalization" is used to convey the hope and determination of order-making on a worldwide scale. It is trumpeted as providing more mobility--of people, capital, and information--and as being equally beneficial for everyone. With recent technological developments--most notably the Internet--globalization seems to be the fate of the world. But no one seems to be in control. As noted sociologist Zygmunt Bauman shows in this detailed history of globalization, while human affairs now take place on a global scale, we are not able to direct events; we can only watch as boundaries, institutions, and loyalties shift in rapid and unpredictable ways. Who benefits from the new globalization? Are people in need assisted more quickly and efficiently? Or are the poor worse off than ever before? Will a globalized economy shift jobs away from traditional areas, destroying time-honored national industries? Who will enjoy access to jobs in the new hierarchy of mobility?
From the way the global economy creates a class of absentee landlords to current prison designs for the criminalized underclass, Bauman dissects globalization in all its manifestations: its effects on the economy, politics, social structures, and even our perceptions of time and space. In a chilling analysis, Bauman argues that globalization divides as much as it unites, creating an ever-widening gulf between the haves and the have-nots. Rather than the hybrid culture we had hoped for, globalization is creating a more homogenous world.
Drawing on the works of philosophers, social historians, architects, and theoreticians such as Michel Foucault, Claude L?vi-Strauss, Alfred J. Dunlap, and Le Corbusier, "Globalization" presents a historical overview of the methods employed to create and define human spaces and institutions, from rural villages to sprawling urban centers. Bauman shows how the advent of the computer translates into the decline of truly public space. And he explores the dimensions of a world in which--through new technologies--time is accelerated and space is compressed, revealing how we have arrived at our current state of global thinking. Bauman's incisive methods of inquiry make "Globalization" an excellent antidote to the exuberance expressed by those who stand to benefit from the new pace and mobility of the modern life."ƒ
¡Ako ne pisheshe Khristo Ianev, a naprimer Tom Klansi ili niakoe drugo ime na izvesten avtor na tril'ri, malko khora shchiakha da se us'mniat dokato chetat. Tova e stremglav eksh'n tril'r, napisan po vsichki pravila na zhanra i naistina se chete na edin d'kh. Deistvieto se razviva v'v Frantsiia i Shveitsariia i glavnite gadni sa frenskiiat premier i podopechniiat mu minist'r na otbranata, koito se zab'rkvat v nezakonni sdelki s or'zhie sreshchu diamanti i podobni.
Dobriiat Rob e v'vlechen sluchaino i ostava sam sreshchu vsichki, kato v kraia vsichkite sa dosta namaleli, a Rob ima nova priiatelka.
Chetiven i mnogo priiaten stil na pisane s chuvstvo za detaila.
Napravo ne e za viarvane, no e istina."ƒ
¡"The Rithmatist, "Brandon Sanderson's "New York Times" bestselling epic teen adventure is now available in paperback.
More than anything, Joel wants to be a Rithmatist. Rithmatists have the power to infuse life into two-dimensional figures known as Chalklings. Rithmatists are humanity's only defense against the Wild Chalklings. Having nearly overrun the territory of Nebrask, the Wild Chalklings now threaten all of the American Isles.
As the son of a lowly chalkmaker at Armedius Academy, Joel can only watch as Rithmatist students learn the magical art that he would do anything to practice. Then students start disappearing--kidnapped from their rooms at night, leaving trails of blood. Assigned to help the professor who is investigating the crimes, Joel and his friend Melody find themselves on the trail of an unexpected discovery--one that will change Rithmatics--and their world--forever.
A "New York Times Book Review "Notable Children's Book of 2013"»
